A||||8||SCCA FIERO||Trunk release hates me?||||1||
Z||000000||SCCA FIERO||08-25-2001||06:44 PM||||My power trunk release stopped working, so I went to fix it. Well, I replaced the switch and solenoid... still wouldn't work. I located the relay and replaced it with the relay from the horn... still didn't work.<P>This is where it get interesting. I jumped the wires where the relay plugs in. I held the plugs so the middle prong was facing up. Then I stuck a wire in the right prong and the center prong and flipped the switch... it works! I can't figure out why the horn relay wouldn't work because the horn works with it in. Am I jumping the wrong wires? The wires are yellow/black, white/black, and the third one - the one not being jumped in my case - is tan/black.<P>Any thoughts?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Joe Torma||08-25-2001||08:09 PM||||Do you have a stick or auto?||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||08-25-2001||08:10 PM||||You've likely got a safety interlock problem.<P>yellow wire... is this automatic? that could mean the neutral safety switch on the tranny is having a snit or the shifter could be out of adjustment a little.||||reg||1
Z||000003||SCCA FIERO||08-25-2001||08:44 PM||||It's a 5 speed.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Rodrv6||08-25-2001||11:28 PM||||Since it's a 5 speed, check and make sure your handbrake switch is working--it's not supposed to release unless the handbrake is set.<P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  84 SE, 330,000 miles and counting, 88 GT, not nearly as many miles :)||||reg||1
Z||000005||DRH||08-26-2001||12:01 AM||||Yep,<P>On mine the wire is tan/white, not tan/black. Anyway, it needs to be grounded for the relay to work. It gets grounded thru the parking brake switch.<P>On mine, the trunk switch will also work with the key off and the brake NOT set. When it does the brake warning light in the dash flashes. I think it feeds back thru the light to ground with the key off. If the bulb is out I assume that feature/bug wouldn't work.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||SCCA FIERO||08-27-2001||10:10 PM||||I checked the handbrake switch... it wasn't connected. It's connected now and the trunk release works with the relay in. BUT now the dinger doesn't stop dinging when the brake is off and the trunk will release when the car is running... it never used to do that. Oh, and the brake light in the dash doesn't come on... don't think it ever has, and I am pretty sure I have checked it in the past when I had the dash apart.||||reg||1
Z||000007||DRH||08-28-2001||01:14 AM||||It sounds like your brake switch is either bad or not adjusted right. It works by grounding the wire running to it when the brake is on. I don't remember exactly what it looks like. Try to look at it while applying/releasing the brake and see if you can make the dinger go off.<P>For the light, start with the bulb. Also try cleaning/adjusting the contacts on the bulb holder to make sure it's making a good connection. I would try to get it fixed since that's the same light that comes on if you have a problem with the hydraulics of the main brakes.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||SCCA FIERO||08-28-2001||08:47 PM||||I fixed it!<P>It was the switch on the parking brake lever. It wasn't adjusted right.||||reg||1
